Based on the provided document (IntarsiaML architecture plan v0.2), here is the section-by-section summary and a list of open questions derived from the "Status vs plan" table and the text.

### Section-by-Section Summary

**0. Goals, Honest Targets, Anti-Goals**
*   **Priorities:** Modularity > Ease of use > Accuracy > Speed (Top 3 per platform) > Reproducibility > APIs > UI > Metrics > Diagrams > Spark/R9700 support > TP > Intel Arc.
*   **Performance Targets:**
    *   **DGX Spark:** Beat llama.cpp/vLLM single-stream; within 10% of TensorFold.
    *   **R9700:** Beat llama.cpp Vulkan/HIP; beat vLLM-radiance (radiance is the long-term bar).
    *   **Apple Silicon:** Correctness only initially.
    *   **Intel Arc:** Out of scope.
*   **Anti-Goals:** No per-family engines (use recipes over shared blocks), no Python in the serving path (native startup speed), no scope sprawl (text LLM inference only, no image/audio/3D), no
